<title>USA: U.S. Dec personal income rose 0.8 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Dec personal income rose 0.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department personal income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Dec    Nov--(Prev)   Oct--(Prev)  Sept</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  0.8    0.6    0.5    0.1   Unch    0.6</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.8    0.6    0.5    0.1    0.1    0.5</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.6    0.4    0.3   -0.2   -0.2    0.3</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.5    0.4    0.5    0.9    0.7    0.1</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.3    0.2    0.3    0.5    0.4   -0.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Dec    Nov--(Prev)   Oct--(Prev)  Sept</p>
<p> Income		   6,639  6,584  6,574  6,544  6,542  6,539</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,744  5,698  5,691  5,664  5,662  5,658</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,434  5,409  5,406  5,386  5,377  5,340</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,266  5,242  5,241  5,220  5,212  5,175</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   638    634    637    634    633    624</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,574  1,564  1,562  1,563  1,559  1,553</p>
<p> -Services		3,054  3,043  3,042  3,023  3,020  2,999</p>
<p> Personal Savings	 310    289    285    278    285    319</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 5.4    5.1    5.0    4.9    5.0    5.6</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Dec    Nov--(Prev)   Oct--(Prev)  Sept</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,755  3,710  3,704  3,682  3,682  3,687</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   693    683    683    680    680    680</p>
<p> -Service Industries  1,324  1,298  1,298  1,285  1,285  1,286</p>
<p> -Government		647    647    646    647    647    647</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    533    532    530    530    529    530</p>
<p> -Farm			 47     49     49     51     51     53</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  485    483    481    480    479    477</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected December personal income to rise 0.8 percent and spending to be up 0.5 percent.</p>
<p>For all of 1996, personal income rose 5.5 percent to 6.453 trillion dollars, while spending rose 2.5 percent to 5.152 trillion dollars. The personal savings rate for 1996 averaged 4.9 percent.  </p>
<p>The Commerce Department said the 0.8 percent rise in December personal income was the largest since the 0.9 percent gain in June of 1996.</p>
